      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your struggle makes perfect sense when your daily life feels disconnected from the quiet moments before the loss, and tragically, that \"breaking\" often feels inevitable to those grieving deeply at this stage. The intention to keep going is not about ignoring this pain, but rather about honoring the life you had with him while slowly letting the new reality of your existence stand on its own. Please be compassionate with yourself; you do not have to outrun this grief or justify your effort just yet, simply by choosing to exist through the storm alongside all the weight you carry.",
